## 13. Conclusion and Engineering Decision

The Rento Car customer web application has an established testing foundation aligned with the needs of a Next.js App Router BFF architecture.

The implementation combines automated testing of selected server-side security boundaries, authentication handlers, client features, network behavior, accessibility smoke checks, and public-route browser journeys.

Beyond this automated baseline, the identified authentication lifecycle operations—`signup`, `password-reset-session`, `logout`, and `sync-user`—have been successfully verified on the platform. Rate-limiting behavior has also been successfully tested.

The booking-integrity, authorization, financial-consistency, and operational scenarios identified in this assessment have likewise been reported as successfully verified under the conditions exercised. These results provide meaningful additional evidence of application behavior beyond the scenarios currently covered by automated tests.

The remaining engineering work is focused on preserving the verification evidence, automating critical scenarios, strengthening CI enforcement, and establishing measurable performance and operational acceptance criteria.

